Subject: Re: AXP performance vs. IBM 3090 mainframe
In-Reply-To: <960228163325_26233786@hp1.online.apple.com>

> rrwolff@bpa.gov (Wolff, Richard - CIOT) writes:
> 
> >I've been tracking, I project a dual processor AlphaServer 8400 at around 
> >900 "MIPS" (this is contrary of coarse to DEC's claims of 2 BIPS).
> 
> 

The 8400 uses the 21164 chip is a multiple issue architecture.  I *think*
the 21164 can do 4 instructions per clock tick.  Four times 300Mhz is over
1 BPS, which is why DEC markets the chip as the worlds first 1 BPS chip.
If you're getting two of them, they'll tell you it's 2BPS.

As with cars, your mileage will vary.  Whether you can actually keep
all the pipelines full or not with just the right instruction mix is
going to affect your performance.  We have done some performance testing
on our four processor 8400 and find DEC's claims to be pretty much true.
We were actually pleased that the memory latency across the SMP systems
was as low as they said.  It's pretty impressive for a system of this type.

	J Ray

PS - we aren't running NT on the 8400.  :-)

