Date: Mon, 4 Mar 1996 16:04:21 -0000
From: Gordon McNab <gordon@fyvie.enet.dec.com>
Subject: RE: display_driver.dll missing

Brian,

Did you replace the failed video card with a different type of card? If =
so, then the
message refers to the fact that the system is trying to use the =
previously installed video driver (probably Compaq Q-Vision) instead of =
the correct driver for the (S3) #9 GXE card.

Normally in Windows NT, to change video card and driver, you install the =
new driver (in control panel -> display) then shutdown, swap the video =
cards, then re-boot. Unfortunately, this is not possible in your case! =
In my opinion the best fix (to avoid re-installing the Operating System) =
would be somehow to get hold of a Compaq Q-Vision card and use it either =
instead of the #9 card or to change the video driver type to S3.

Gordon

