From donald@wreath.ENET.dec.com Tue Mar  5 12:16:52 1996 CST
Message-ID: <9603051741.AA02782@us1rmc.bb.dec.com>
Date: Tue, 5 Mar 96 13:00:05 EST
From: think pc Think PC THINK PC! <donald@wreath.ENET.dec.com>
Subject: Re: Adding ISA board to Alpha XL

>I am now wondering if I have to configure anything before being able to 
>add an ISA board. One of the DEC supplied help files mentions an ISA 
>Configuration Utility but I cannot find such a prog either on the HD or 
>on any of the provided floppies and CDs. Does anyone have a clue what 
>this might be?
>
>TIA

    Hi,
    
    The ISA config utility (ISACFG) is used with the SRM firmware (for
    the OpenVMS and Digital UNIX operating systems). The Alpha XL runs
    ARC firmware (for Windows NT), and does not have a firmware-based
    ISA config utility. 

    When configuring the ISA option make sure there are no conflicts
    with other devices. ARC and Windows NT preassign some IRQs for PCI
    devices as follows:

	IRQ 10 PCI slot 1
	IRQ 15 PCI slot 2
	IRQ  9 PCI slot 3
	IRQ 11 Embedded SCSI controller

    This leaves IRQ 5 and 14 available for devices in the ISA slots.
    Also, you might be able to free up IRQ 3 by disabling COM2.

    Regards,
    Terry

