Subject: RE: Adding ISA board to Alpha XL

Pedro,

The ISA configuration file is something required for Digital UNIX or
OpenVMS.  Windows Nt doesn't use one, and you shouldn't have to do anything
special to configure any ISA device, other than to manually make sure you
don't have IRQ, DMA channel, or I/O address clashes.

The most likely problem you will encounter with the SoundBlaster is that it
wants IRQ 5, by default, and you may have another device that wants the same
IRQ, e.g., some network interfaces do.

Cheers,
James

