At 10:58 am 03/06/96 -0600, Zoromski, Brian wrote:
>Does anyone have any experience (good or bad) with DEC's TZ88 Digital
>Linear Tape Drive?  The cartridges say they store 20/40 GB w/
>compression; has anyone used one?
>

The DLT tape drives are truly awesome -- with our UltraBac software we have
seen (on uniprocessor machines!) over 130Mb/Min backup rates.  One of our
customers has even reported 95Mb/Min across his network.  The most important
thing to realize with DLT compared to helical scan technology (4mm/8mm) is
that the tape drive heads to not actually come into contact with the media.
This means that the media is rated for use 1,000 times longer than DAT.
Unfortunately, the media is five times the price of DAT media, but per MB of
storage the cost is the same.  The DLT drives we have had in here for
evaluation (including some autoloader models) have proven themselves to be
very reliable.

