From: Aaron Sakovich <(no email)>
Subject: Re: 40 GB Linear tape drive
In-Reply-To: <19960306200727211.AAA179@HOLLY>

> The DLT tape drives are truly awesome -- with our UltraBac software we have
> seen (on uniprocessor machines!) over 130Mb/Min backup rates.  One of our
> customers has even reported 95Mb/Min across his network.  The most important
> thing to realize with DLT compared to helical scan technology (4mm/8mm) is
> that the tape drive heads to not actually come into contact with the media.

Well, not exactly true, but close.  While 8mm heads contact the media for
270 degrees around the head (remember, these tape drives were designed for
video recording, hence the helical scan design), and 4mm hits for about 90
degrees, the DLT's contact patch is only 2 degrees.  This is where the
name comes from, also -- Linear recording, as opposed to helical scan.

Cheers,
Aaron

