> 
> even towels." Thats why we should always release csp v x.1.3 -- trap the
> unwary.
> 
> ___

As far as I've heard is this a problem with the implementation
of Java in Netscape 2.0. So it's OK to use if you disable Java.

Probably what happends when you use Java is that when you access 
a www page is that it could send you a Java script. This script 
is executed on your local machine with your rights and therefore 
can access all files and information that you have the rights to 
access. As I said probably something like this.

