With all the chatter about Netscape on Alpha systems, here's a new one:  I just 
purchased the 1.22 version from Digital for "Windows '95 / Windows NT for 
Digital Alpha Systems".  I tried the 2.0 version for Windows '95/NT (that 
Netscape's salesperson assured me would work fine on an Alpha system - it 
didn't) and the setup program wouldn't even run.  I returned the 2.0 version
to Netscape, and just received the 1.22 version from Digital.  Setup ran 
smoothly; but when I tried to run Netscape, it generated an error message 
indicating that several .dll files were missing.  I called Digital's tech 
support line and they told me that their version also had missing .dll's and 
that Netscape knows about the problem.  (The .dll's aren't on the distribution 
disks!)  Digital told me that their fix was to go to Netscape's web site and 
download a "test drive" package of the server version and get the .dll's from 
it.  I tried this, but the 'netscape.cgi' file wouldn't decompress regardless 
of the filename.  (You're told that if you request .zip compression, you must 
rename the .cgi file to "communications.ntalpha.zip" in order to decompress 
it.)Has anyone else had this problem?  Digital suggested I contact Netscape's 
tech
support, which I did, but so far to no avail.  I also tried Microsoft's 
internet browser, but got the same error message that someone else on this 
mail list reported.  (The error regarding the entry point in the page setup 
.dllno found.)  I would welcome any suggestions. . .I'd really like to start 
using my internet access at home :\

