From mspence@eastman.com Mon Mar 11 21:36:45 1996 CST
Message-ID: <2.2.32.19960313033306.007a54e4@stc150.kpt.emn.com>
Date: Tue, 12 Mar 1996 22:33:06 -0500
From: Michael H. Spence <mspence@eastman.com>
Subject: NT SMTP/POP3 Servers

I have been trying to evaluate various SMTP/POP3 servers for our Alpha
Windows/NT boxes.  We are primarily a VAX/VMS shop with people using Eudora
for e-mail access.  I would like to move a number of these individuals to
the Alpha NT servers and have them pick up their mail there.  We are
separated from the internet by a firewall and all messages that go outside
of our local domain (*.kpt.emn.com or *.emn.com) must pass through this
firewall.

So far I have looked at:

(1) NT-MAIL from the Internet Shopper. 
     - Alpha Version available
     - Could never get the software to pick up accounts from the domain
       I had to add POP accounts manually
     - Seemed to be able to handle routing for internal/external mail

(2) IMS - EMWAC Internet Mail Services
     - Alpha Version available
     - Price is right
     - Does not handle smart SMTP routing.  All SMTP mail had to be forwarded
       to an internal host that could handle the routing

(3) Post.Office - Software.Com
     - No Alpha Version (intel/mips)
     - Looks like it requires separate POP account 
     - Will handle routing records

(4) Microsoft Exchange Server
     - Alpha Version available
     - Does not appear to provide POP3 services, requires Exchange client

Does anyone know of other SMTP/POP3 programs for the Alpha platform that are
not on this list?  So far, I'm leaning towards the IMS program from EMWAC. It
handles all my needs except for smart SMTP routing.

Thanks...
