>
>I need to route domain logons from windows for workgroups machines
>via an ISDN (64k) link to an NT server. There are approximately 55
>satellite sites with 2 or 3 machines (tops) at each site...     so
>installing NT servers at each site is out of the question. Similarly,
>there is a need to be able to view each site from the central site
>(which doesn't happen across the link with just workgroup/username/
>password set up properly - only server connections are visible)...
>To add to this, SMS will be set up in the near future for help-desk
>capability as well as inventory control, which may have problems in
>the current configuration.
>
>There are only currently two sites running, but without domain logon
>or the ability to view remote sites from the central site.
>
>I believe I have seen a similar discussion somewhere previously, but
>I have checked my archives (& MSDN & TechNet) and have not been able
>to find the solution. If anyone knows of a suitable config, please
>e-mail me... (all suggestions valued)
>
>Thanx in Advance
>Dave.
>
>Technical Info:
>Links are brought up-down on an as-needed basis.
>Links only route IP traffic (no bridging).
>Hardware for the ISDN link is CISCO 1003 IP only at remotes,
>  CISCO 7010 at central.
>PING, TELNET, NET USE etc all work accross link (even when link
>  is down to start).
>File Manager - Connect Network Drive can browse the NT Server
>  only after machine name is given.
>No DNS server exists, all LMHOSTS files are set up correctly.
>Windows for Workgroups has ONLY MS TCP/IP stack installed on DEC 
>  EWRKS3 network card.
>Windows for Workgroups Domain Logon appears to send a broadcast
>  to the local network. It is impossible to bridge this as is is
>  sent to the local ethernet ONLY (x.x.2.255) and even turning
>  bridging all protocols and multicasts and broadcasts on on the 
>  router did not result in a valid logon (this was tried with
>  both link down before - by waiting for timeout - and with link
>  active before - and hence during - logon through ping prior).
>In all configurations:
>  Starting Windows for Workgroups brings link to UP status.
>  Logging off whilst running Windows for Workgroups does not
>    change status of link.
>  Logging on whilst running Windows for Workgroups does not
>    change status of link.
>  PING, TELNET, NET USE etc work.
>
>Sample Config:
>
>             PC             C1003                   C7010          Server
>IP         x.x.2.1        x.x.2.245               x.x.1.245       x.x.1.150
>N/M     255.255.255.0   255.255.255.0           255.255.255.0   255.255.255.0
